       peated requests (that require expensive rreeqquueesstt--kkeeyy(8) upcalls)  for  a
       key that can’t (at the moment) be positively instantiated.

       Once the key has been instantiated, the authorization key (KKEEYY__SSPPEECC__RREE‐‐
       QQKKEEYY__AAUUTTHH__KKEEYY)  is  revoked,  and the destination keyring (KKEEYY__SSPPEECC__RREE‐‐
